SCOPE OF THE ABOVE

The MIT licence above covers only what the 1.6 port added:

  - the six patch files as rewritten: the class name they all used had been
    renamed upstream, two Alpha Animals defs no longer exist, the operations
    were regrouped so one failure no longer silences the rest, and the mod
    guards now test defs instead of display names
  - LoadFolders.xml, rewritten and renamed
  - the packaging and the documentation

IT DOES NOT COVER THE ORIGINAL MOD. The idea, the split between "no bone" and
"no bone and no fat", and Hiroyan's lists of seventy-five Alpha Animals
creatures sorted into those two groups, are SirMashedPotato's and Hiroyan's:

  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2041677515

They never declared a licence for it, so none is granted here and none can be.
It is redistributed under the usual practice for abandoned mods - explicit
credit, a link to the original, and removal on request.

If SirMashedPotato or Hiroyan asks for this to be taken down, it comes down.
Immediately, and without discussion.

ATTRIBUTION.md records what was taken and what was changed.
